public class TrickyArrays{
    public static void main(String[] args){
        var i = 0;
        int[] iA = {10, 20};
        iA[i] = i = 30; //Tricky part
        System.out.println(""+ iA[0] + "" + iA[1] + "" + i);
    }
}
//Explanation:
// In the line iA[i] = i = 30;, the assignment is evaluated from right to left.
// First, i is assigned the value 30.
// Then, iA[i] is evaluated. At this point, i has already been updated to 30.
// However, the original value of i (which was 0) is used to determine the index for iA, because array indexing is done before the assignment.
// Therefore, iA[0] is assigned the value 30.